<title>CANADA: Bombardier board okays 70-seat jet plan.</title>
<headline>Bombardier board okays 70-seat jet plan.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombardier Inc said on Tuesday its board authorized the Aerospace Group to proceed with the launch of the Canadair airliner CRJ-X, the 70-seat extension of the current 50-passenger regional jet.</p>
<p>The Aerospace Group will make a formal announcement with full details of the program in the third week of February, Bombardier said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
